<div class="mc mc-prose">
  <p class="mc-note"><b>Effective date:</b> November 11, 2026</p>

  <p>This policy explains what information {{ site.legalName }} ("RaeAligned," "I," "me") collects through raealignedservices.com, how I use it, and the choices you have. It covers RaeAligned Strategic Services and its division, {{ site.division }}.</p>

  <h3>What I collect</h3>
  <p><b>Information you send me.</b> When you use the contact form, I receive your name, email address, and the message you write, plus your phone number and topic if you choose to include them.</p>
  <p>When you use the notary request form, I also receive the address where the signing will take place, your preferred date and time, the type of document, the number of signatures and signers, any notes you add, and your confirmation of the photo-ID and travel-fee terms.</p>
  <p><b>Information you share by email or booking.</b> If you email me or book an appointment, I receive what you include, such as your contact details and appointment information.</p>
  <p><b>Technical information.</b> Like most websites, the host keeps standard server logs, such as IP addresses and browser type, for security and to keep the site running. This site does not use advertising cookies, tracking pixels, or analytics tools that follow you across other websites.</p>

  <h3>How I use it</h3>
  <ul class="mc-list">
    <li>To reply to your message or question.</li>
    <li>To schedule, prepare for, and carry out the appointment or service you asked for, including travel to a signing location.</li>
    <li>To keep the records North Carolina requires of notaries, where they apply.</li>
    <li>To protect the site and its forms from spam and misuse.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>I don't sell your information, and I don't share it with anyone for their marketing. I won't add you to a mailing list unless you ask to be added.</p>

  <h3>Services that handle your information</h3>
  <p>I use a few trusted services to run the site and my business. Each one handles your information under its own privacy policy:</p>
  <ul class="mc-list">
    <li><b>Netlify</b> hosts this website and receives form submissions, which are delivered to my business email.</li>
    <li><b>Google Appointment Schedules</b> handles consultation bookings.</li>
    <li><b>Square Appointments</b> may handle notary bookings and payments.</li>
    <li><b>My business email provider</b> stores the messages you send.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>I may also share information if the law requires it, such as in response to a valid legal request.</p>

  <h3>Links to other sites</h3>
  <p>This site links to my Instagram and Facebook pages and to booking pages run by the services above. Those sites have their own privacy practices, which this policy doesn't cover.</p>

  <h3>How long I keep it</h3>
  <p>I keep your information only as long as I need it for the purposes above, or longer where the law requires it, such as notary record-keeping. Form submissions I no longer need are deleted.</p>

  <h3>How I protect it</h3>
  <p>The site uses HTTPS encryption, and access to form submissions and email is protected by password. No method of sending or storing information online is completely secure, so please don't send sensitive documents or ID images through the website forms. Bring them to your appointment instead.</p>

  <h3>Your choices</h3>
  <p>You can ask me what information I hold about you, ask me to correct it, or ask me to delete it, unless I'm required to keep it. Email <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a> and I'll respond within a reasonable time.</p>

  <h3>Children</h3>
  <p>This site and my services are meant for adults. I don't knowingly collect information from children under 13. If you believe a child has sent me information, email me and I'll delete it.</p>

  <h3>Changes to this policy</h3>
  <p>If I change this policy, I'll post the new version here and update the effective date at the top.</p>

  <h3>Contact</h3>
  <p>{{ site.legalName }}<br>Raleigh–Durham, North Carolina<br><a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a></p>
</div>
